I don't think of it as cheating. As ais523 described, the same thing 
happens with other graphical versions - including the official version - 
and the colour of the ascii graphics conveys some of the same info as 
well. So... I don't see it as cheating because it's essentially written 
into the rules of the game. At worst, it's 'exploiting a bug'; and this 
particular bug is essentially impossible to avoid.

There really should be generic graphics for that kind of stuff. Blind 
players should not be able to see the colour of potions. But the way the 
game is currently written makes it difficult to put in special graphics 
to deal with the problem.

